WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:17.892 --> 00:00:20.395
She would’ve thought two
years was enough time for the

00:00:20.395 --> 00:00:22.480
strangeness to rub off, but it wasn’t.

00:00:25.025 --> 00:00:29.612
Julianne Moore is an 
amazingly talented actress.

00:00:29.612 --> 00:00:31.781
She’s an Academy
Award winning actress,

00:00:32.949 --> 00:00:37.996
and when she expressed
enthusiasm for the story

00:00:37.996 --> 00:00:40.749
and the script, I was just overjoyed.

00:00:40.749 --> 00:00:41.708
I was over the moon.

00:00:42.709 --> 00:00:44.919
Julianne is so powerful.

00:00:44.919 --> 00:00:49.299
She has not only a very particular
beauty, but is someone that can

00:00:49.299 --> 00:00:52.385
hold an enormous amount of mystery.

00:00:53.803 --> 00:00:56.723
And I think when you work
with materials like this,

00:00:57.766 --> 00:01:02.353
with mystery, suspense, fantasy,
thriller, you know, they're all

00:01:02.353 --> 00:01:07.400
mixed and combined in this
sort of explosion of memories.

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:11.112
Someone like Julianne can really
hold it and pull it together.

00:01:11.821 --> 00:01:15.366
It’s a hugely challenging part because
she’s playing somebody who's

00:01:15.366 --> 00:01:19.996
full of grief and full of pain and
often under threat in the thing.

00:01:19.996 --> 00:01:24.167
So it’s a very sort of heightened
state she’s in throughout.

00:01:26.711 --> 00:01:31.007
Time apparently did nothing but
blunt grief’s sharpest edge,

00:01:31.007 --> 00:01:33.468
so that it hacked rather than sliced.

